## Provider Authentication

The OCI provider supports several authentication methods. Choose one — the
provider block in `main.tf` does **not** need credentials hardcoded.

### Option 1 — `~/.oci/config` file (recommended for local dev)

If you have already run `oci setup config` or the OCI CLI is configured,
no changes are needed. The provider reads the `[DEFAULT]` profile automatically.

To use named profiles (useful when primary and DR are in the same tenancy but
you want explicit control):

```ini
# ~/.oci/config
[DEFAULT]
tenancy     = ocid1.tenancy.oc1..aaa
user        = ocid1.user.oc1..bbb
fingerprint = aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff:00:11:22:33:44:55:66:77:88:99
key_file    = ~/.oci/oci_api_key.pem
region      = {{ primary_oci_region }}

[DR]
tenancy     = ocid1.tenancy.oc1..aaa
user        = ocid1.user.oc1..bbb
fingerprint = aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:ff:00:11:22:33:44:55:66:77:88:99
key_file    = ~/.oci/oci_api_key.pem
region      = {{ standby_oci_region }}
```

Then add `config_file_profile` to the provider blocks in `main.tf`:

```hcl
provider "oci" {
  alias               = "primary"
  region              = var.primary_region
  config_file_profile = "DEFAULT"
}

provider "oci" {
  alias               = "dr"
  region              = var.dr_region
  config_file_profile = "DR"
}
```

### Option 2 — Variables (explicit, good for teams)

```hcl
# variables.tf (add these)
variable "tenancy_ocid"      { type = string; sensitive = true }
variable "user_ocid"         { type = string; sensitive = true }
variable "fingerprint"       { type = string; sensitive = true }
variable "private_key_path"  { type = string }
```

```hcl
# main.tf — update provider blocks
provider "oci" {
  alias            = "primary"
  region           = var.primary_region
  tenancy_ocid     = var.tenancy_ocid
  user_ocid        = var.user_ocid
  fingerprint      = var.fingerprint
  private_key_path = var.private_key_path
}

provider "oci" {
  alias            = "dr"
  region           = var.dr_region
  tenancy_ocid     = var.tenancy_ocid
  user_ocid        = var.user_ocid
  fingerprint      = var.fingerprint
  private_key_path = var.private_key_path
}
```

```bash
# terraform.tfvars — keep out of git
tenancy_ocid     = "ocid1.tenancy.oc1..xxx"
user_ocid        = "ocid1.user.oc1..xxx"
fingerprint      = "aa:bb:cc:..."
private_key_path = "~/.oci/oci_api_key.pem"
```

Or via environment variables:

```bash
export TF_VAR_tenancy_ocid="ocid1.tenancy.oc1..xxx"
export TF_VAR_user_ocid="ocid1.user.oc1..xxx"
export TF_VAR_fingerprint="aa:bb:cc:..."
export TF_VAR_private_key_path="~/.oci/oci_api_key.pem"
```

### Option 3 — Inline private key (CI/CD)

```hcl
variable "private_key_content" { type = string; sensitive = true }

provider "oci" {
  alias        = "primary"
  region       = var.primary_region
  tenancy_ocid = var.tenancy_ocid
  user_ocid    = var.user_ocid
  fingerprint  = var.fingerprint
  private_key  = var.private_key_content
}
```

```bash
export TF_VAR_private_key_content="$(cat ~/.oci/oci_api_key.pem)"
```

### Option 4 — Instance Principal (OCI Compute / OCI DevOps)

```hcl
provider "oci" {
  alias  = "primary"
  region = var.primary_region
  auth   = "InstancePrincipal"
}
```

