## Deploy

### Option A — Single apply (Terraform handles ordering)

```bash
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply
```

Terraform runs `module.primary` and `module.dr` in parallel, then automatically
waits for both before applying `module.drg_peering`.

### Option B — Staged apply (recommended for first-time setup)

```bash
# Stage 1 — provision both regions (verify networking before peering)
terraform apply -target=module.primary -target=module.dr

{% if not manage_route_table %}
# After Stage 1: add DG route rules manually — see Route Table Management above

{% endif %}
# Stage 2 — activate cross-region DRG peering
terraform apply -target=module.drg_peering

# Stage 3 — full apply to reconcile any remaining drift
terraform apply
```

